{
  "specVersion": "0.1.0",
  "about": "The authoritative list of OpenLogo's built-in names for this specification version: every keyword and every primitive, aliases included. spec/grammar.md:363 governs them with one rule -- a program may not DECLARE a built-in name, and may BIND a value to any name -- and spec/grammar.md:414 versions them with the specification. This file is that list in machine-readable form, and CI asserts the implementation's registries equal it exactly, in both directions (docs/adr/0021-built-in-names-list-and-ci-gate.md). It is normative and maintainer-owned like the rest of spec/. Membership here answers one question only -- may a program declare this name? -- and never how a word is highlighted, which spec/tooling.md owns as an independent axis.",
  "invariants": {
    "unconditional": "Every profile's keywords and primitives are built-in names in EVERY implementation, whether or not that profile is claimed (spec/grammar.md:408). `profile` below is metadata for docs and tooling; nothing may branch on it when deciding whether a name is blocked at a declaration slot.",
    "precedence": "A name reachable from two registries is filed ONCE, as `keyword` before `primitive`, and its `profile` follows the precedence-winning registry -- so `to` is core-language, not heritage. Precedence runs in the key order of `registries` below. The full membership is always recorded in `registries` on the entry, never inferred from `category` or `profile`, so losing one of two registrations fails the gate instead of matching a summary that still looks right.",
    "bothDirections": "The gate compares structured entries, not a flat name set: every name here must be in the implementation and every name in the implementation must be here, with `category`, `profile` and `registries` all checked. Each registry names TWO accessors because the two directions need different shapes -- a `lookup` (is this name here?) and an `enumerate` (what does this hold?). The eight *PrimitiveArity functions are lookups only.",
    "accessorStatus": "`present` means the accessor MUST resolve as a public export of @openlogo/parser; a missing one is drift. `declared` means decided but not yet created: the gate accepts its absence and FAILS if it ever resolves, because at that moment it should have become `present`. Status attaches per accessor, not per tag, because a tag can be split. At 0.1.0 every accessor is `present`.",
    "derivedEnumeration": "The nine profile-keyed primitive tags enumerate through ONE accessor, `profilePrimitiveNames`, called with the tag's own profile. Nine hand-written per-profile enumerators would each be a claim about a registry, maintained by hand, beside the registry -- the shape this whole file exists to remove. The derived form also lets the gate sweep OL_CHECK_PROFILES directly, so a TENTH profile that gains a primitive table is covered with no edit to this file at all."
  },
