  "profiles": {
    "about": "The profile inventory, tying three surfaces together. The NORMATIVE inventory is spec/conformance.md's own profile sections (ADR-0021 §3 clause 2), the implementation's is OL_CHECK_PROFILES, and this map is what makes them comparable. It is data rather than derived because the two spellings do not correspond mechanically -- `Interaction & Events` and `Tutor (AI)` do not become `interaction-events` and `tutor-ai` by any rule a reader could reconstruct -- so a guessed transformation would be a hand-maintained claim wearing an algorithm's clothes. Gated in BOTH directions: a profile added to spec/conformance.md with no checker id fails, and a checker id with no section fails.",
    "ids": {
      "core-language": "Core Language",
      "turtle-rendering": "Turtle & Rendering",
      "geometry": "Geometry",
      "data": "Data",
      "heritage": "Heritage",
      "sprites": "Sprites",
      "interaction-events": "Interaction & Events",
      "sound": "Sound",
      "modules": "Modules",
      "localization": "Localization",
      "educational": "Educational",
      "tutor-ai": "Tutor (AI)"
    }
  },
  "profilesWithoutPrimitives": {
    "modules": "The Modules profile's surface is the Core keywords `import` and `export` plus module resolution; it introduces no primitive of its own (spec/conformance.md's Modules section). ADR-0021 §5 additionally forbids a loaded library's procedures from ever entering this list -- they register through the ordinary phase-1 procedure table, so colliding with one raises ol-duplicate-definition, not ol-reserved-word.",
    "localization": "Localization ships `alias` keyword packs -- alternate spellings declared in OpenLogo source -- rather than primitives (spec/conformance.md's Localization section). An alias spelling a program declares is a program name, not a built-in one."
  },
  "tokenClassKeyword": {
    "about": "spec/tooling.md's `keyword` TOKEN CLASS is a different set from the keyword list above, on purpose (spec/grammar.md:378). It cannot be derived: measured against shipped output it OMITS some keywords, ADDS some words that are not built-in names at all, and adds the profile words. Both a positional rule (falsified by `local end`, `export end` and `:p.end` all emitting `keyword`) and \"the keyword list minus the operators\" (which would re-derive paint from the declaration list, forbidden by spec/grammar.md:378) were tried and refuted by measurement in issue #855. So it is an enumeration in prose -- and an enumeration needs a gate. Only the DELTAS live here; the membership is computed from them, so this is not a second list to keep in step. Deliberately no counts in this sentence: the counts are `omitsKeywords.length` and `addsExcluded.length`, and stating them here would be exactly the hand-maintained restatement the deltas exist to avoid.",
    "omitsKeywords": [
      "and",
      "or",
      "not",
      "mod"
    ],
    "omitsReason": "The word-spelled operators of the expression grammar. They are keywords -- a program may not declare them -- and they are painted `operator`, which is exactly the independence spec/grammar.md:378 states.",
    "addsExcluded": [
      "empty",
      "member",
      "of",
      "a"
    ],
    "addsExcludedReason": "The four contextual words. They are not built-in names, yet they take this class in the structural positions recorded in `excluded[].positions`, and are ordinary names everywhere else.",
    "addsProfileKeywords": true,
    "addsProfileKeywordsNamedIndividually": [
      "tell"
    ],
    "rowAnchors": {
      "exclusionClause": "The word-spelled operators",
      "exclusionPolarity": "are **not** in this class",
      "profileClause": "while their profile is active, the profile block-heads together with the Sprites mode-switch command `tell`",
      "deltaSentence": "it omits {omits} reserved words, adds {adds} non-reserved ones",
      "independenceClause": "This class is **not derived from** the reserved list"
    },
    "rowAnchorsReason": "The gate splits the row at `exclusionClause` and compares BOTH segments by set equality: the enumeration before it must name exactly the computed membership, and the words inside the clause must be exactly `omitsKeywords`. Every other anchor guards a claim the segments cannot see. `exclusionPolarity` and `independenceClause` are POLARITY claims -- rewriting \"are **not** in this class\" to \"are in this class\", or \"**not derived from**\" to \"derived from\", inverts a rule while every gated token stays identical. `profileClause` carries the words \"while their profile is active\" for the same reason: gating the noun phrase and not its condition would let the paint axis be made unconditional silently. `deltaSentence` is a TEMPLATE, not a sentence: the counts are filled in from `omitsKeywords` and `addsExcluded`, so the prose cannot state a number this file does not hold. A one-directional check -- every expected word appears somewhere in the row -- was measured GREEN against five mutations including `polygon` added to the class, which is why all of this exists.",
    "addsProfileKeywordsReason": "The profile block-heads and the Sprites mode-switch command `tell` take this class while their profile is active. That is the PAINT axis and is unaffected by these words being built-in names unconditionally on the DECLARATION axis. The row names `tell` individually because it is not a block head, and defers to the profile documents for the block-head NAMES rather than restating them -- so `addsProfileKeywordsNamedIndividually` records the ones set equality must expect, and `rowAnchors.profileClause` gates the deferral. Restating the six block-heads here would be the third list to keep in step that spec/grammar.md:414 warns against."
  },
